<h1>Register</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Registration &gt; Register</b></span> <i><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:normal;">or it will be automatically launched as second step of the registration process (right after</span> <span class="Command">Pick Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:normal;">+ drag&amp;drop operation)</span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Register</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command aligns two different surfaces in such a way so their common areas coincide. It works with scan data. mesh and point clouds entities.</span></p>
<p>Call the <span class="Command">Register</span> command and the following dialog will appear:</p>
<p><img src="../images/Registration_21.gif" width="384px" height="261px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>From Document</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select the document where the scanned data will be taken from.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>To Document</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Select the document where the scanned data will be inserted.</p>
<p>In both listboxes the number in brackets indicates how many feature points have been set in the referent document. If the numbers in the selected documents are different, the button 'Go!' will remain not active and the registration will not start.</p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If the registration is automatically started after drag&amp;drop, both '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>From Document</b></span>' and '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>To Document</b></span>' listboxes will be set correctly.</p>
<p class="sub-head">On Registering group:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Options regarding the way, that registered data should be handled.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Copy and paste data</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Will take the data from the source file and paste it into the target file but without closing the source file.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cut and paste data</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Will take the data form the source document, paste it in the target document and close the source document without saving it.</p>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> The number of feature points in both documents should be the same. The number of feature points captured can be seen on the top right corner of the document.</p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">I</span><font style="font-family:Arial;" face="Arial">f the software fails to find the proper transformation, there will be an error message: "<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Can not register entities. Please change or delete feature points and try again.</b></span>". Change the picked feature points by using the command <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick Feature Points</b></span> and try again to register the entities.</font></p>
<p class="whs5">If you need to adjust both entities manually, then use the command <span class="Command">Rotate and Translate</span>.</p>
